SUMMARY:NAMIWalks Yolo County
DESCRIPTION:Hope is on the move. Residents across Yolo County are coming together for the\nannual NAMIWalks Yolo County\, part of the nation’s largest and most vibrant mental health\nawareness event series. \nThis year’s theme\, “Together We Are NAMIWalks\,” reflects the strength\, connection\, and\ncompassion of our community. Every step taken and every dollar raised fuels NAMI’s free\nprograms\, advocacy\, and support services – making a lasting difference for the 1 in 5 who\nexperience mental health conditions each year. \nNAMIWalks is more than a walk: it’s a movement. Participants leave inspired\, empowered\, and\nreminded that no one is ever alone. Together\, we are stronger. Together\, we create hope.\nTogether\, we are NAMIWalks. \nWHAT: NAMIWalks Yolo County\nWHERE: Woodland Community College | 2300 Gibson Rd\, Woodland\, CA 95776\nEvent Route Length: 1k and 5K routes\nWHEN: Saturday\, September 26\, 2026 \n“The need has never been greater to build community support so we can realize Mental Health for\nAll in our lifetime” said Executive Director Lou Enge. “The impact of NAMIWalks is deeply felt\, in\nfamilies\, workplaces\, schools\, and neighborhoods. This event is a reminder of our values that\nwhen we work together— we are unstoppable.” \nTo participate in NAMIWalks\, register at namiwalks.org/yolocounty. There is no registration fee\,\nbut fundraising is encouraged (and essential!). Participants raising $100 or more receive the official\n2026 event T-shirt. Every dollar raised stays local\, powering NAMI Yolo County’s free\, top-rated\nmental health programs\, education\, and support.
URL:https://thedirt.online/event/namiwalks-yolo-county/
LOCATION:Woodland Community College\, 2300 E Gibson Rd.\, Woodland\, CA\, 95776
CATEGORIES:Athletics,Bring the Kids,Community,Featured,Fitness,Outside
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://thedirt.online/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Email-Header.jpg
END:VEVENT
